The history of this repository was rewritten and replaced on the remote by a forced push. Your clone still has the old history. Do not push your old branches back: that would bring the old commits back.

Branch main on origin: abababababab -> cdcdcdcdcdcd
  No local work on it:
    git fetch origin
    git checkout main
    git reset --hard origin/main
  Local commits on top of the old main:
    git fetch origin
    git rebase --onto origin/main abababababab main

Tag v1.2 on origin: 121212121212 -> 343434343434
  Replace your copy:
    git fetch origin +refs/tags/v1.2:refs/tags/v1.2

Other branches of yours that contain old commits keep them until you rebase them onto the new history. The ids above and the commit map tell which.
